Alkali-Aggregate Reactivity Facts Book — FHWA (@mat-aar: 0, is #reference, #part-of @mat-sources) { r_1RPCXTH7BRN45SFFG6XC76WZNK
M. D. A. Thomas, B. Fournier and K. J. Folliard, *Alkali-Aggregate Reactivity (AAR) Facts Book*, FHWA-HIF-13-019, March 2013. [Official publication](https://www.fhwa.dot.gov/pavement/pub_details.cfm?id=894), [preserved full GovInfo PDF](https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/GOVPUB-TD2-PURL-gpo41382/pdf/GOVPUB-TD2-PURL-gpo41382.pdf).

Read the whole book progressively: reaction chemistry, symptoms, tests, prevention, specifications, diagnosis/prognosis, mitigation and alkali-carbonate reaction. Publication details, complete contents and selected diagnosis passages were inspected on 30 October 2026. The report lists 211 pages; this does not imply that every table or case was inspected. Distinguish several possible causes of cracking and seek corroborating petrography and exposure evidence.

The government report is publicly distributed without access restrictions; preserve authors and separately credited components. Standards cited are historical references, not a verified current specification. Keep the PDF external. This book deeply covers AAR, not every concrete durability mechanism.

